concepts.statement:
An ultrafilter \(\mathcal{F}\) satisfies

 • \(A \cap B \in \mathcal{F} if and only if A \in \mathcal{F}
 \text{ and } B \in \mathcal{F}\).

 • \(A \cup B \in \mathcal{F} if and only if A \in \mathcal{F}
 \text{ or } B \in \mathcal{F}\).

 • \(A^c \in \mathcal{F} if and only if A \notin \mathcal{F}\).

($\varepsilon$-steadiness). A sequence ${a_n}$ is $\varepsilon$-steady iff each pair $a_i, a_j$ is infinitesimally-close for every $i, j \in \mathbb{N}$. In other words,
\begin{align*}
{a_n} \text{ is } \varepsilon\text{-steady} &if and only if a_i \simeq a_j \\
&if and only if d(a_i, a_j) \leq \varepsilon \cdot a \\
\end{align*}
$\forall \text{ } i, j \in \mathbb{N}$.

