concepts.statement:
(Infinitely-close sequences). Let ${a_n}$ and ${b_n}$ be two sequences. We say that ${a_n}$ is infinitely-close (or $\varepsilon$-close) to ${b_n}$ iff $a_n$ is infinitely-close to $b_n$ for each $n\in \mathbb{N}$. In other words, 
\begin{align*}
 {a_n} \text{ is infinitely-close to } {b_n} & if and only if d(a_n, b_n) \leq \varepsilon \cdot c = \frac{1}{\Omega} \cdot c \\
 & if and only if a_n \simeq b_n,
\end{align*}
for all $n \in \mathbb{N}, c \in \mathbb{Q}^+$.

