concepts.statement:
(Equivalent sequences). Two sequences ${a_n}$ and ${b_n}$ are equivalent iff they are eventually infinitely-close. In other words,
\begin{align*}
 {a_n} \text{ and } {b_n} \text{ are equivalent } & if and only if d(a_n, b_n) = |a_n - b_n| \leq \varepsilon \cdot c = \frac{1}{\Omega} \cdot c \\
 & if and only if a_n \simeq b_n
\end{align*}
for all $n \geq \Omega, c \in \mathbb{Q}^+$.

